                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "85e8658e-cf43-3713-9d75-74489574fb10",
                        "entry_id": "5eb7a654-7b70-3190-82fe-0cd1b8b04141",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative form of Leonese."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "95f23e11-9a83-4748-8bcc-3da5f43be9f6",
                                "sense_id": "85e8658e-cf43-3713-9d75-74489574fb10",
                                "text": "But, as in Somoza’s life, the potent Leónese family of Sánchez interceded."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "71b2d6f9-f28f-4b31-9d48-1787363983cb",
                                "sense_id": "85e8658e-cf43-3713-9d75-74489574fb10",
                                "text": "The gates, towers, walls and most Leónese residences were destroyed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d113678-4142-4861-b3f3-02687027e920",
                                "sense_id": "85e8658e-cf43-3713-9d75-74489574fb10",
                                "text": "The following year Muslim armies plundered the Tagus valley while Leónese forces, working in co-operation with the Caliph al-Mansur and the kingdom of Navarre, attacked from the west."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "906987a1-2abb-3651-b7a0-be9fd824c391",
                        "entry_id": "5eb7a654-7b70-3190-82fe-0cd1b8b04141",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of, from or relating to the city of León, León department, Nicaragua."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ecd00d8b-9e5f-4f7c-ac86-12a9b3970756",
                                "sense_id": "906987a1-2abb-3651-b7a0-be9fd824c391",
                                "text": "Without going into the political complications in Central America, suffice it to say that Cole had concluded that the liberal government which had granted his contract in Honduras would probably fall if the liberal Leónese revolution of the Democrats failed in Nicaragua."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d8f19bd3-1719-4ae6-9bcd-37d5758138fd",
                                "sense_id": "906987a1-2abb-3651-b7a0-be9fd824c391",
                                "text": "What makes this museum opposite Ruinas San Sebastián unmissable is the striking contrast of its main subjects: a quirky collection of life-size papier-mâché figures from Leónese history and legend, handmade by founder Señora Toruña (also represented in glorious papier-mâché), and murals graphically depicting methods the National Guard used to torture prisoners."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "80a1d914-3fb1-47f6-a898-8239316ccb23",
                                "sense_id": "906987a1-2abb-3651-b7a0-be9fd824c391",
                                "text": "A hero, for his ideals, a pariah for his failures, the important thing was that he occupied the attentions and affections of the Leónese community whom he came to emblemize on the world stage played out in Central American affairs of state."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "4b747f5f-80af-33ab-b73a-01a7a11535fb",
                "word": "Leónese",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "906338c1-8599-46c1-a1e8-44dfae4da821",
                        "entry_id": "4b747f5f-80af-33ab-b73a-01a7a11535fb",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Leónese"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5304e711-f581-3676-b944-32ac3becc10c",
                        "entry_id": "4b747f5f-80af-33ab-b73a-01a7a11535fb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative form of Leonese."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9ee9ca1-8ba4-4f21-9190-2fc07bfc370b",
                                "sense_id": "5304e711-f581-3676-b944-32ac3becc10c",
                                "text": "He then took the rest of the country, making the Leónese and General Jérez his junior partners. The Leónese were willing to remain faithful to Walker as long as he could keep their enemies the Granadans in check."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0254ec34-d4b6-4c97-963f-3e43a1f9b82e",
                                "sense_id": "5304e711-f581-3676-b944-32ac3becc10c",
                                "text": "We were set upon by seven or more Leónese."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d9701da-76f1-4e44-8698-509c4da1c83c",
                                "sense_id": "5304e711-f581-3676-b944-32ac3becc10c",
                                "text": "With his departure, Alfonso VIII was free to vent his wrath on the Leónese who were themselves under immense pressure from the papacy to desist from attacking their Christian neighbours."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "942a1b2d-978c-3949-b014-698f5a2bf7bb",
                        "entry_id": "4b747f5f-80af-33ab-b73a-01a7a11535fb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A native or inhabitant of the city of León, León department, Nicaragua."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9240bb6-1794-4811-af44-51c1fa998b5c",
                                "sense_id": "942a1b2d-978c-3949-b014-698f5a2bf7bb",
                                "text": "In 1853 a Nicaraguan president, a Leónese, died a natural death in office (itself an unheard-of occurrence), and in the election that followed, the winner was Fruto Chamorro, the most belligerent of that Granada clan."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f11cb5f-c6fe-4fd9-9409-0510db99a5eb",
                                "sense_id": "942a1b2d-978c-3949-b014-698f5a2bf7bb",
                                "text": "I remain staggered by the warmth and generosity shown me by so many Nicaraguans, particularly the Leónese, who were always willing to take the time to explain the subtle intricacies of daily life in Nicaragua to a less-than-subtle North American."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3609389-f100-460c-9943-32c2564902f1",
                                "sense_id": "942a1b2d-978c-3949-b014-698f5a2bf7bb",
                                "text": "Regional forces were already involved in the conflict, with Guatemalan Conservatives assisting the Granadans and Salvadorian Liberals assisting the Leónese."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
